{
  "title": "3Sum",
  "difficulty": "Medium",
  "patterns": [
    "two-pointers"
  ],
  "js": [
    "sorting",
    "arrays"
  ],
  "order": 4,
  "summary": "List every unique triplet of numbers that adds up to zero.",
  "fn": "threeSum",
  "params": [
    "nums"
  ],
  "types": {
    "params": [
      "number[]"
    ],
    "returns": "number[][]"
  },
  "compare": "deep-unordered",
  "tests": [
    {
      "args": [
        [
          -1,
          0,
          1,
          2,
          -1,
          -4
        ]
      ],
      "expected": [
        [
          -1,
          -1,
          2
        ],
        [
          -1,
          0,
          1
        ]
      ],
      "explain": "Two different triplets sum to 0. [-1, 0, 1] can be made with either -1, but it is listed once. The order of triplets, and of numbers inside a triplet, doesn't matter."
    },
    {
      "args": [
        [
          0,
          1,
          1
        ]
      ],
      "expected": [],
      "explain": "The only triplet sums to 2."
    },
    {
      "args": [
        [
          0,
          0,
          0
        ]
      ],
      "expected": [
        [
          0,
          0,
          0
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "args": [
        [
          0,
          0,
          0,
          0
        ]
      ],
      "expected": [
        [
          0,
          0,
          0
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "args": [
        [
          -2,
          0,
          1,
          1,
          2
        ]
      ],
      "expected": [
        [
          -2,
          0,
          2
        ],
        [
          -2,
          1,
          1
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "args": [
        [
          1,
          2,
          -2,
          -1
        ]
      ],
      "expected": []
    },
    {
      "args": [
        [
          3,
          0,
          -2,
          -1,
          1,
          2
        ]
      ],
      "expected": [
        [
          -2,
          -1,
          3
        ],
        [
          -2,
          0,
          2
        ],
        [
          -1,
          0,
          1
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "args": [
        [
          -4,
          -2,
          -2,
          -2,
          0,
          1,
          2,
          2,
          2,
          3,
          3,
          4,
          4,
          6,
          6
        ]
      ],
      "expected": [
        [
          -4,
          -2,
          6
        ],
        [
          -4,
          0,
          4
        ],
        [
          -4,
          1,
          3
        ],
        [
          -4,
          2,
          2
        ],
        [
          -2,
          -2,
          4
        ],
        [
          -2,
          0,
          2
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "args": [
        [
          -1,
          0,
          1,
          0
        ]
      ],
      "expected": [
        [
          -1,
          0,
          1
        ]
      ]
    }
  ],
  "hints": [
    "Fix one number, nums[i]. Now you need two other numbers that add up to -nums[i]. Which earlier problem is that?",
    "Sort first. Then for each i, run the opposite-ends two-pointer search on the part of the array to the right of i.",
    "To avoid duplicate triplets, skip an i whose value equals the previous i's value, and after a match move both pointers past equal values."
  ],
  "complexity": {
    "time": "O(n²): n choices of i, each with an O(n) two-pointer walk (the O(n log n) sort is smaller)",
    "space": "O(1) extra besides the output (O(log n) to O(n) for the sort, depending on the engine)"
  }
}
